      "content": "that's pretty intense. when you say \"impartial judgment\" to check \"systemic power\" and stop people from \"privileging a single identity,\" it sounds like you're leaning into a specific political viewpoint. some people would argue that the most important virtue is actually personal responsibility or tradition—the idea that respecting established norms and individual accountability is what keeps a society from falling apart. how do you reconcile your list with those more traditional, conservative values? are they just not \"heavy-hitting\" enough for what you're describing?",
